1. An oil supply structure for a planetary gear device, comprising:  

a rotating tubular body configured to rotate about an axis and including an internal oil passage through which lubricating oil is supplied;  

an annular oil supply member disposed radially outward of the rotating tubular body and having an oil supply port configured to receive the lubricating oil from an oil source;  

a first seal ring and a second seal ring disposed between an outer peripheral surface of the rotating tubular body and an inner peripheral surface of the annular oil supply member, the first seal ring and the second seal ring being spaced apart in an axial direction to define, between the rotating tubular body and the annular oil supply member, an annular oil chamber communicating with the oil supply port and the internal oil passage;  

at least one bypass passage configured to provide fluid communication from the annular oil chamber to a region outside the annular oil chamber while bypassing at least one of the first seal ring and the second seal ring; and  

at least one pressure reduction mechanism provided in the at least one bypass passage and configured to reduce pressure of lubricating oil flowing through the at least one bypass passage,  

wherein the annular oil chamber is configured to supply the lubricating oil to the planetary gear device through the internal oil passage of the rotating tubular body, and  

wherein the at least one bypass passage and the at least one pressure reduction mechanism are configured to suppress an increase in pressure in the annular oil chamber acting on the first seal ring and the second seal ring during rotation of the rotating tubular body.
